e flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-5" dir="auto" data-message-author-role="assistant" data-message-id="f59a4461-cb86-4ccf-8d1f-a25ef6ee5aee" data-message-model-slug="gpt-4o"><div class="flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[3px]"><div class="markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words light"><p class="" data-start="82" data-end="477">French fries are a significant product in the global food trade, involving exports, imports, tariffs, market competition, and various trade regulations. This article provides a detailed analysis of the international trade of French fries. we will look at the trade data, key export/import countries, regulations, and price trends to help food traders and importers make informed decisions.</p><hr class="" data-start="479" data-end="484" /><h2 class="" data-start="486" data-end="550"><span class="ez-toc-section" id="1_Why_Are_People_Searching_for_%E2%80%9CFrench_Fries_HS_Code%E2%80%9D"></span><strong data-start="489" data-end="548">1. Why Are People Searching for “French Fries HS Code”?</strong><span class="ez-toc-section-end"></span></h2><p class="" data-start="551" data-end="958">If you are likely trying to:<br data-start="627" data-end="630" /><img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.0.3/svg/2705.svg" decoding="async" class="emoji" role="img" draggable="false" alt="✅" title="French Fries HS Code 20041000: More Useful Information for Importers 36"> <strong data-start="632" data-end="655">Import French fries</strong> and need to understand customs classifications, tariffs, and clearance procedures.<br data-start="738" data-end="741" /><img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.0.3/svg/2705.svg" decoding="async" class="emoji" role="img" draggable="false" alt="✅" title="French Fries HS Code 20041000: More Useful Information for Importers 36"> <strong data-start="743" data-end="766">Export French fries</strong> and want insights into target market regulations and competitors.<br data-start="832" data-end="835" /><img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.0.3/svg/2705.svg" decoding="async" class="emoji" role="img" draggable="false" alt="✅" title="French Fries HS Code 20041000: More Useful Information for Importers 36"> <strong data-start="837" data-end="862">Monitor market trends</strong> to analyze global supply chains and pricing before making purchasing or investment decisions.</p><p class="" data-start="960" data-end="1275">It is important to mesmerize the French Fries HS Code <strong>20041000</strong><br data-start="975" data-end="978" />Bad example: A Chinese food distributor planned to import <strong data-start="1023" data-end="1052">French fries from Belgium</strong>, using HS Code <strong data-start="1068" data-end="1080">20041000</strong> for frozen potato products. However, the company was unaware of <strong data-start="1145" data-end="1186">China’s CIQ food safety certification</strong> requirements, leading to customs clearance delays and disruptions in its supply chain.</p><hr class="" data-start="1277" data-end="1282" /><h2 class="" data-start="1284" data-end="1344"><span class="ez-toc-section" id="2_Top_Exporters_of_French_Fries_Latest_2024_Data"></span><strong data-start="1287" data-end="1342">2. Top Exporters of French Fries (Latest 2024 Data)</strong><span class="ez-toc-section-end"></span></h2><p class="" data-start="1345" data-end="1483">According to <strong data-start="1358" data-end="1437">2023 data from the International Trade Centre (ITC) and World’s Top Exports</strong>, the leading exporters of French fries are:</p><div class="overflow-x-auto contain-inline-size"><table border="1" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2" data-start="1485" data-end="1879"><thead data-start="1485" data-end="1585"><tr data-start="1485" data-end="1585"><th data-start="1485" data-end="1496"><strong data-start="1487" data-end="1495">Rank</strong></th><th data-start="1496" data-end="1520"><strong data-start="1498" data-end="1519">Exporting Country</strong></th><th data-start="1520" data-end="1558"><strong data-start="1522" data-end="1557">2023 Export Value (Billion USD)</strong></th><th data-start="1558" data-end="1585"><strong data-start="1560" data-end="1583">Global Market Share</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody data-start="1652" data-end="1879"><tr data-start="1652" data-end="1695"><td>1</td><td><strong data-start="1658" data-end="1669">Belgium</strong> <img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.0.3/svg/1f1e7-1f1ea.svg" decoding="async" class="emoji" role="img" draggable="false" alt="🇧🇪" title="French Fries HS Code 20041000: More Useful Information for Importers 39"></td><td><strong data-start="1677" data-end="1685">5.78</strong></td><td>24.2%</td></tr><tr data-start="1696" data-end="1743"><td>2</td><td><strong data-start="1702" data-end="1717">Netherlands</strong> <img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.0.3/svg/1f1f3-1f1f1.svg" decoding="async" class="emoji" role="img" draggable="false" alt="🇳🇱" title="French Fries HS Code 20041000: More Useful Information for Importers 40"></td><td><strong data-start="1725" data-end="1733">4.35</strong></td><td>18.2%</td></tr><tr data-start="1744" data-end="1785"><td>3</td><td><strong data-start="1750" data-end="1760">Canada</strong> <img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.0.3/svg/1f1e8-1f1e6.svg" decoding="async" class="emoji" role="img" draggable="false" alt="🇨🇦" title="French Fries HS Code 20041000: More Useful Information for Importers 41"></td><td><strong data-start="1768" data-end="1776">2.31</strong></td><td>9.7%</td></tr><tr data-start="1786" data-end="1834"><td>4</td><td><strong data-start="1792" data-end="1809">United States</strong> <img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.0.3/svg/1f1fa-1f1f8.svg" decoding="async" class="emoji" role="img" draggable="false" alt="🇺🇸" title="French Fries HS Code 20041000: More Useful Information for Importers 42"></td><td><strong data-start="1817" data-end="1825">2.24</strong></td><td>9.4%</td></tr><tr data-start="1835" data-end="1879"><td>5</td><td><strong data-start="1841" data-end="1854">Argentina</strong> <img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.0.3/svg/1f1e6-1f1f7.svg" decoding="async" class="emoji" role="img" draggable="false" alt="🇦🇷" title="French Fries HS Code 20041000: More Useful Information for Importers 43"></td><td><strong data-start="1862" data-end="1870">1.32</strong></td><td>5.5%</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 class="" data-start="1881" data-end="1949"><span class="ez-toc-section" id="Why_Are_Belgium_and_the_Netherlands_the_Largest_Exporters"></span><strong data-start="1885" data-end="1947">Why Are Belgium and the Netherlands the Largest Exporters?</strong><span class="ez-toc-section-end"></span></h3><p class="" data-start="1950" data-end="2284"><img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.0.3/svg/1f539.svg" decoding="async" class="emoji" role="img" draggable="false" alt="🔹" title="French Fries HS Code 20041000: More Useful Information for Importers 44"> <strong data-start="1953" data-end="1984">Superior Potato Cultivation</strong> – These countries have ideal conditions for high-starch potatoes, perfect for French fries.<br data-start="2076" data-end="2079" /><img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.0.3/svg/1f539.svg" decoding="async" class="emoji" role="img" draggable="false" alt="🔹" title="French Fries HS Code 20041000: More Useful Information for Importers 44"> <strong data-start="2082" data-end="2116">Advanced Processing Technology</strong> – Cutting-edge frozen food processing facilities ensure high quality.<br data-start="2186" data-end="2189" /><img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.0.3/svg/1f539.svg" decoding="async" class="emoji" role="img" draggable="false" alt="🔹" title="French Fries HS Code 20041000: More Useful Information for Importers 44"> <strong data-start="2192" data-end="2228">Strong Logistics &amp; Supply Chains</strong> – Efficient ports make global exports cost-effective.</p><p class="" data-start="2286" data-end="2573"><strong data-start="2286" data-end="2301">Case Study:</strong><br data-start="2301" data-end="2304" />In 2023, <strong data-start="2313" data-end="2340">Belgian company Agristo</strong> exported over <strong data-start="2355" data-end="2396">1 million tons of frozen French fries</strong>, with <strong data-start="2403" data-end="2437">50% destined for Asian markets</strong> (China, Japan, South Korea). Strategic partnerships with fast-food chains like McDonald’s and Burger King boosted their global reach.</p><hr class="" data-start="2575" data-end="2580" /><h2 class="" data-start="2582" data-end="2642"><span class="ez-toc-section" id="3_Top_Importers_of_French_Fries_Latest_2024_Data"></span><strong data-start="2585" data-end="2640">3. Top Importers of French Fries (Latest 2024 Data)</strong><span class="ez-toc-section-end"></span></h2><p class="" data-start="2643" data-end="2802">The demand for frozen French fries is increasing worldwide, particularly in <strong data-start="2719" data-end="2747">Asia and the Middle East</strong>. The largest importers of French fries in 2023 were:</p><div class="overflow-x-auto contain-inline-size"><table border="1" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2" data-start="2804" data-end="3196"><thead data-start="2804" data-end="2904"><tr data-start="2804" data-end="2904"><th data-start="2804" data-end="2815"><strong data-start="2806" data-end="2814">Rank</strong></th><th data-start="2815" data-end="2839"><strong data-start="2817" data-end="2838">Importing Country</strong></th><th data-start="2839" data-end="2877"><strong data-start="2841" data-end="2876">2023 Import Value (Billion USD)</strong></th><th data-start="2877" data-end="2904"><strong data-start="2879" data-end="2902">Global Market Share</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody data-start="2971" data-end="3196"><tr data-start="2971" data-end="3020"><td>1</td><td><strong data-start="2977" data-end="2994">United States</strong> <img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.0.3/svg/1f1fa-1f1f8.svg" decoding="async" class="emoji" role="img" draggable="false" alt="🇺🇸" title="French Fries HS Code 20041000: More Useful Information for Importers 42"></td><td><strong data-start="3002" data-end="3010">3.04</strong></td><td>14.5%</td></tr><tr data-start="3021" data-end="3064"><td>2</td><td><strong data-start="3027" data-end="3038">Germany</strong> <img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.0.3/svg/1f1e9-1f1ea.svg" decoding="async" class="emoji" role="img" draggable="false" alt="🇩🇪" title="French Fries HS Code 20041000: More Useful Information for Importers 48"></td><td><strong data-start="3046" data-end="3054">2.16</strong></td><td>10.3%</td></tr><tr data-start="3065" data-end="3105"><td>3</td><td><strong data-start="3071" data-end="3080">Japan</strong> <img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.0.3/svg/1f1ef-1f1f5.svg" decoding="async" class="emoji" role="img" draggable="false" alt="🇯🇵" title="French Fries HS Code 20041000: More Useful Information for Importers 49"></td><td><strong data-start="3088" data-end="3096">1.98</strong></td><td>9.5%</td></tr><tr data-start="3106" data-end="3146"><td>4</td><td><strong data-start="3112" data-end="3121">China</strong> <img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.0.3/svg/1f1e8-1f1f3.svg" decoding="async" class="emoji" role="img" draggable="false" alt="🇨🇳" title="French Fries HS Code 20041000: More Useful Information for Importers 50"></td><td><strong data-start="3129" data-end="3137">1.87</strong></td><td>8.9%</td></tr><tr data-start="3147" data-end="3196"><td>5</td><td><strong data-start="3153" data-end="3171">United Kingdom</strong> <img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.0.3/svg/1f1ec-1f1e7.svg" decoding="async" class="emoji" role="img" draggable="false" alt="🇬🇧" title="French Fries HS Code 20041000: More Useful Information for Importers 51"></td><td><strong data-start="3179" data-end="3187">1.62</strong></td><td>7.7%</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 class="" data-start="3198" data-end="3248"><span class="ez-toc-section" id="Why_Are_These_Countries_Major_Importers"></span><strong data-start="3202" data-end="3246">Why Are These Countries Major Importers?</strong><span class="ez-toc-section-end"></span></h3><p class="" data-start="3249" data-end="3607"><img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.0.3/svg/2705.svg" decoding="async" class="emoji" role="img" draggable="false" alt="✅" title="French Fries HS Code 20041000: More Useful Information for Importers 36"> <strong data-start="3251" data-end="3268">United States</strong> – Although the US produces its own French fries, it imports large quantities from <strong data-start="3351" data-end="3381">Canada and the Netherlands</strong> to meet demand.<br data-start="3397" data-end="3400" /><img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.0.3/svg/2705.svg" decoding="async" class="emoji" role="img" draggable="false" alt="✅" title="French Fries HS Code 20041000: More Useful Information for Importers 36"> <strong data-start="3402" data-end="3432">Germany, Japan, and the UK</strong> – Strong fast-food industries drive consistent demand.<br data-start="3487" data-end="3490" /><img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.0.3/svg/2705.svg" decoding="async" class="emoji" role="img" draggable="false" alt="✅" title="French Fries HS Code 20041000: More Useful Information for Importers 36"> <strong data-start="3492" data-end="3501">China</strong> – Rapid growth in quick-service restaurants (KFC, Pizza Hut, and local chains) fuels increased imports.</p><p class="" data-start="3609" data-end="3899"><strong data-start="3609" data-end="3624">Case Study:</strong><br data-start="3624" data-end="3627" />In 2023, <strong data-start="3636" data-end="3690">China imported over 1 million tons of French fries</strong>, <strong data-start="3692" data-end="3755">with more than 50% sourced from Belgium and the Netherlands</strong>. As frozen food consumption rises in second-tier and third-tier cities, China’s demand for imported French fries is expected to keep growing.</p><hr class="" data-start="3901" data-end="3906" /><h2 class="" data-start="3908" data-end="3970"><span class="ez-toc-section" id="4_Trade_Details_Tariffs_Regulations_and_Logistics"></span><strong data-start="3911" data-end="3968">4. Trade Details: Tariffs, Regulations, and Logistics</strong><span class="ez-toc-section-end"></span></h2><h3 class="" data-start="3972" data-end="4024"><span class="ez-toc-section" id="Import_Tariffs_for_French_Fries_2024_Rates"></span><strong data-start="3976" data-end="4024">Import Tariffs for French Fries (2024 Rates)</strong><span class="ez-toc-section-end"></span></h3><ul data-start="4025" data-end="4309"><li class="" data-start="4025" data-end="4059"><p class="" data-start="4027" data-end="4059"><strong data-start="4027" data-end="4036">China</strong>: 10% tariff + 9% VAT</p></li><li class="" data-start="4060" data-end="4086"><p class="" data-start="4062" data-end="4086"><strong data-start="4062" data-end="4071">Japan</strong>: 8.5% tariff</p></li><li class="" data-start="4087" data-end="4146"><p class="" data-start="4089" data-end="4146"><strong data-start="4089" data-end="4098">India</strong>: 30% tariff (to protect domestic agriculture)</p></li><li class="" data-start="4147" data-end="4235"><p class="" data-start="4149" data-end="4235"><strong data-start="4149" data-end="4167">European Union</strong>: Zero tariffs within the EU (Belgium/Netherlands have free trade)</p></li><li class="" data-start="4236" data-end="4309"><p class="" data-start="4238" data-end="4309"><strong data-start="4238" data-end="4255">United States</strong>: 0% tariff from <strong data-start="4272" data-end="4282">Canada</strong>, 8% from other countries</p></li></ul><h3 class="" data-start="4311" data-end="4356"><span class="ez-toc-section" id="Food_Safety_Labeling_Requirements"></span><strong data-start="4315" data-end="4354">Food Safety &amp; Labeling Requirements</strong><span class="ez-toc-section-end"></span></h3><p class="" data-start="4357" data-end="4688"><img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.0.3/svg/1f4cc.svg" decoding="async" class="emoji" role="img" draggable="false" alt="📌" title="French Fries HS Code 20041000: More Useful Information for Importers 55"> <strong data-start="4360" data-end="4369">China</strong> – Requires CIQ (China Inspection and Quarantine) approval and compliance with <strong data-start="4448" data-end="4483">GB 2760 food additive standards</strong>.<br data-start="4484" data-end="4487" /><img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.0.3/svg/1f4cc.svg" decoding="async" class="emoji" role="img" draggable="false" alt="📌" title="French Fries HS Code 20041000: More Useful Information for Importers 55"> <strong data-start="4490" data-end="4508">European Union</strong> – Products must follow <strong data-start="4532" data-end="4563">HACCP food safety standards</strong> and label allergens.<br data-start="4584" data-end="4587" /><img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.0.3/svg/1f4cc.svg" decoding="async" class="emoji" role="img" draggable="false" alt="📌" title="French Fries HS Code 20041000: More Useful Information for Importers 55"> <strong data-start="4590" data-end="4605">Middle East</strong> – Countries like Saudi Arabia require <strong data-start="4644" data-end="4667">Halal certification</strong> for imported food.</p><h3 class="" data-start="4690" data-end="4733"><span class="ez-toc-section" id="Cold_Chain_Logistics_Requirements"></span><strong data-start="4694" data-end="4731">Cold Chain Logistics Requirements</strong><span class="ez-toc-section-end"></span></h3><ul data-start="4734" data-end="5028"><li class="" data-start="4734" data-end="4826"><p class="" data-start="4736" data-end="4826">French fries must be <strong data-start="4757" data-end="4781">transported at -18°C</strong> to maintain quality and prevent oxidation.</p></li><li class="" data-start="4827" data-end="5028"><p class="" data-start="4829" data-end="5028"><strong data-start="4829" data-end="4857">Port storage regulations</strong>: Import hubs like <strong data-start="4876" data-end="4927">Shanghai Port (China) or Jebel Ali Port (Dubai)</strong> require frozen goods to be stored in designated cold storage facilities to avoid clearance delays.</p></li></ul><hr class="" data-start="5030" data-end="5035" /><h2 class="" data-start="5037" data-end="5100"><span class="ez-toc-section" id="5_Market_Price_Trends_for_French_Fries_2024_Q1_Data"></span><strong data-start="5040" data-end="5098">5. Market Price Trends for French Fries (2024 Q1 Data)</strong><span class="ez-toc-section-end"></span></h2><p class="" data-start="5101" data-end="5257">French fries’ prices are influenced by <strong data-start="5140" data-end="5217">weather conditions, logistics costs, and global supply chain fluctuations</strong>. As of early 2024, price trends were:</p><div class="overflow-x-auto contain-inline-size"><table border="1" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="2" data-start="5259" data-end="5666"><thead data-start="5259" data-end="5377"><tr data-start="5259" data-end="5377"><th data-start="5259" data-end="5283"><strong data-start="5261" data-end="5282">Exporting Country</strong></th><th data-start="5283" data-end="5318"><strong data-start="5285" data-end="5317">2023 Average Price (USD/ton)</strong></th><th data-start="5318" data-end="5348"><strong data-start="5320" data-end="5347">2024 Q1 Price (USD/ton)</strong></th><th data-start="5348" data-end="5377"><strong data-start="5350" data-end="5375">Year-over-Year Change</strong></th></tr></thead><tbody data-start="5457" data-end="5666"><tr data-start="5457" data-end="5506"><td><strong data-start="5459" data-end="5470">Belgium</strong> <img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.0.3/svg/1f1e7-1f1ea.svg" decoding="async" class="emoji" role="img" draggable="false" alt="🇧🇪" title="French Fries HS Code 20041000: More Useful Information for Importers 39"></td><td><strong d