000: More Useful Information for Importers 42"></td><td><strong data-start="5638" data-end="5645">730</strong></td><td><strong data-start="5648" data-end="5655">765</strong></td><td><img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.0.3/svg/1f53a.svg" decoding="async" class="emoji" role="img" draggable="false" alt="🔺" title="French Fries HS Code 20041000: More Useful Information for Importers 59">4.8%</td></tr></tbody></table></div><h3 class="" data-start="5668" data-end="5704"><span class="ez-toc-section" id="Why_Are_Prices_Increasing"></span><strong data-start="5672" data-end="5702">Why Are Prices Increasing?</strong><span class="ez-toc-section-end"></span></h3><p class="" data-start="5705" data-end="6009"><img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.0.3/svg/1f4c8.svg" decoding="async" class="emoji" role="img" draggable="false" alt="📈" title="French Fries HS Code 20041000: More Useful Information for Importers 66"> <strong data-start="5708" data-end="5734">Higher Logistics Costs</strong> – Rising fuel prices impact transportation expenses.<br data-start="5787" data-end="5790" /><img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.0.3/svg/1f4c8.svg" decoding="async" class="emoji" role="img" draggable="false" alt="📈" title="French Fries HS Code 20041000: More Useful Information for Importers 66"> <strong data-start="5793" data-end="5821">Potato Yield Variability</strong> – Weather conditions affect supply; droughts in some regions cause shortages.<br data-start="5899" data-end="5902" /><img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.0.3/svg/1f4c8.svg" decoding="async" class="emoji" role="img" draggable="false" alt="📈" title="French Fries HS Code 20041000: More Useful Information for Importers 66"> <strong data-start="5905" data-end="5932">Rising Fast-Food Demand</strong> – Increased consumption in <strong data-start="5960" data-end="5988">Asia and the Middle East</strong> keeps prices high.</p><hr class="" data-start="6011" data-end="6016" /><h2 class="" data-start="6018" data-end="6037"><span class="ez-toc-section" id="Conclusion"></span><strong data-start="6021" data-end="6035">Conclusion</strong><span class="ez-toc-section-end"></span></h2><p class="" data-start="6038" data-end="6439">French fries are a growing global trade commodity, with <strong data-start="6094" data-end="6134">Belgium, the Netherlands, and the US</strong> dominating exports, while <strong data-start="6161" data-end="6190">China, Japan, and Germany</strong> lead in imports. <strong data-start="6208" data-end="6273">Understanding tariffs, food safety regulations, and logistics</strong> is crucial for businesses looking to enter this market. Keeping an eye on <strong data-start="6348" data-end="6388">price trends and demand fluctuations</strong> helps optimize purchasing and export strategies.</p><p class="" data-start="6441" data-end="6610"><img src="https://s.w.org/images/core/emoji/15.0.3/svg/1f680.svg" decoding="async" class="emoji" role="img" draggable="false" alt="🚀" title="French Fries HS Code 20041000: More Useful Information for Importers 69"> <strong data-start="6444" data-end="6610" data-is-last-node="">If you’re a food trader looking to source high-quality French fries or expand into export markets, contact us for more market insights and business opportunities!</strong></p></div></div></div></div>`} />
